The AMZN pillar check returned no change and the projection check found no matching modeled year, so the remaining question is whether any claim raises a debate that no pillar covers. The email's GAAP EPS of $2.46 against $1.92 consensus rests on a modeled $7.4bn non-operating gain, and none of the AMZN pillars (AWS re-acceleration, retail margin, capex conversion) mentions non-operating gains or earnings quality. That permits one spawn_new_thesis call for AMZN, limited to the gain and EPS claims.

